[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   Step 105 -- third-catalogue bidirectional replication + map transfer.
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   The transit evidence rests on the Warsaw and CODE cohorts, which are
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   independent in sample but share the Poznan orbit-determination
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   lineage.  The one-apparition catalogue (Krolikowska 2014, A&A 571,
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   A63; VizieR J/A+A/571/A63) supplies a third population: comets
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   observed at a single apparition, orbit-fitted on the shortest arcs
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   the catalogues carry, with osculating / original / future solutions
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   plus MW08 comparison 1/a values.  None of these comets entered the
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   slip map's construction.
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   This step runs the entire transit instrument on that cohort
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   end-to-end: the identical REBOUND/IAS15 + DE440s bidirectional
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   integration to the 250 AU barycentric sphere, the catalogue
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   boundary solutions reproduced as validation, the planetary-subtracted
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   implied proper-time slip derived with the step-065 conversion, and
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   then -- the discriminating test -- whether the bipolar slip map
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   fitted on the 229 Warsaw+CODE comets predicts this third cohort's
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   unexplained slip out-of-sample.
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   T1  machinery validation: simulated vs catalogue boundary
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   periapsis directions per leg (the step-063 instrument check).
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   T2  channel replication: in-cap vs out-cap contrast of the
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   unexplained slip, and the continuous theta correlation, on
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   the new cohort alone.
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   T3  map transfer: the map dtau = a + b*cos(2*theta) fitted on the
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   229 (step 102, frozen coefficients) predicts the lpc cohort's
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   dtau_unexplained -- Spearman, sign accuracy, and predicted vs
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   observed median in each of the three map regions.
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   T4  MW08 cross-lineage energy channel on the same cohort
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   (the only MW08 observable; MW08 publishes no angular
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   elements), reported for completeness.
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   The cohort is small (n ~ 30-40 after the spike cut), so the test is
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   powered for sign and amplitude consistency rather than a fresh
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   detection; results are reported at face value with the sample size
[2026-09-20 12:19:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 105]   stated.  Fixed seeds throughout.
